A||||3||Mattyman||Tell of your funny fiero stories||||10||
Z||000000||Mattyman||09-17-2001||12:18 AM||||Just wanted to hear about funny things that happened to you guys while crusin your Fiero's in the snow and if anyone had any good races lately.||||reg||10
Z||000001||onfire||09-17-2001||12:35 AM||||My friend spun a bearing in the 85 GT I used to own. While doing doughnuts in the snow around a box of kittens. O.K. there were no kittens, but he still blew up my motor. lol I now have another 85 GT, and he's not driving this one. Besides he has his own know.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000002||Ferrari_cdn||09-18-2001||07:24 PM||||When I drove my new Fiero up to my girlfriend's house, (they never saw it yet), then she came out to take a look.  Her father came out then and took a look.  He wanted to look under the front hood so I popped open the hood.  He was standing in front of the car.  I said, not there, but here while I open it the other way.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Then when he saw under the hood, he had this WTF look, wondering where the heck my engine is.  He was looking at it from some angles, noting my radiator in the front.  He even tried to look from under the car!  My girlfriend, who already knew where it is, was laughing.  I was playing along and told him that I don't have one.  He looked at me.  "Lets see under the trunk".  When he saw the vents, he knew then.  I opened the trunk and he then thought it was cool.<P>It was funny.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1984 2m4<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||09-18-2001||11:04 PM||||This ones kind of funny, last winter in my fiero I was out with a friend doing a bunch of donuts at this big dead intersection. This was right after it snowed like 2 inchs of fresh powder. Anyways after doing a bunch of spin outs and leaving obviously noticeable marks I did one last big one. I ended up making the car slide backwards and it stalled out on me. So basicly im stalled in the middle of the intersection sideways with multiple donut marks. Then a I see headlights approaching me. Well it ends up being a cop. I finally get the car started and slowly drive away expecting to be pulled over. The cop folowed me for a few miles. But never pulled me over. Needless to say I was happy. Even if he did stop me, he'd probably just give me a warning. But I really dont like being stoped by cops whatever the reason.<P>The same things happend with me speeding a few times, as with everybody else im sure. But this was just a had to be there situation.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I had a good laugh after this happend.<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||10
